WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.467 --> 00:00:06.398
Automations do routine work for you. Each one has a trigger, when it runs, and an action, what it does.

2
00:00:07.102 --> 00:00:14.718
Open Automations in the sidebar. Each automation shows its trigger, the next run and the last run, grouped by project.

3
00:00:15.424 --> 00:00:20.011
New automation opens a wizard in three steps: When, What and Details.

4
00:00:20.709 --> 00:00:30.778
When can be a time, something that happens in a project, an incoming ticket or e-mail, or only when you run it. Here: on a schedule, weekdays at seven in the morning.

5
00:00:31.483 --> 00:00:40.187
What is the action. Create a card is the most common; it can also ask DevOps, ask the CEO, send a webhook or e-mail a digest.

6
00:00:40.887 --> 00:00:46.284
Details names the automation and fills in the card it creates: the project and the title.

7
00:00:46.989 --> 00:00:53.048
Create automation saves it. Run now runs it once, straight away: here it creates the card at once.

8
00:00:53.748 --> 00:00:58.591
History lists every run: what triggered it, on schedule or by hand, and what it did.

9
00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:03.834
Pause switches an automation off without deleting it. Resume turns it back on.

10
00:01:04.534 --> 00:01:08.075
That is Automations. Set up the routine once, and let it run.
